From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:23:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] notificationmanager: visibility of notifications per view, lock screen hints
Description:
 Applications could not keep the content of a notification off the lock
 screen, and a shell had no way to show less than everything.
 .
 A view sets how much its model shows (Notifications.visibility):
 everything, only the sender (the summary of messages, categories im,
 email and call, or a public summary the application gives, and the
 image of a message as the avatar), only the application, or nothing. On
 the lock screen (Notifications.lockScreen) the visibility configured per
 application and the one a notification asks for apply as well; the
 strictest wins. A new proxy model leaves out hidden notifications and
 empties the roles with content (summary, body, image, actions, urls,
 hints); VisibilityRole tells the view what it may show.
 .
 New hints: x-kde-lock-screen-visibility (full, sender, application,
 hidden; an unknown value hides) and x-kde-public-summary. Portal
 notifications map hide-on-lock-screen and hide-content-on-lock-screen,
 read the category, priority urgent becomes critical (it was unreachable)
 and the display hint is read under its specified name display-hint.
 .
 New settings: LockScreenVisibility (default only the sender),
 PopupVisibility and HistoryVisibility (default everything), and
 LockScreenVisibility per application.
 .
 Notifications.source WatcherSource mirrors the notifications of the
 server over D-Bus through the same model, for a lock screen in another
 process.
Author: masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
License: LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-28
